1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:50,717
Let's say Mikoy's intel is valid.

2
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,511
The next question is, is it actionable?

3
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:56,514
If we don't act now
and go to Italy right away,

4
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,683
we'll end up wasting the intel we have.

5
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:03,396
What guarantee do we have
that this mission will be successful?

6
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:08,109
What guarantee do we have
that we'll all make it back alive?

7
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:17,327
<i>I failed Mikoy,</i>

8
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,953
<i>but definitely,</i>

9
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:22,248
<i>I cannot let my mission fail.</i>

10
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,008
I hope this mission can change you back.

11
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:34,135
As much as my brain can't imagine

12
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:36,429
you and Chiara getting back together,
but you know,

13
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:38,556
I'm genuinely rooting for the two of you.

14
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,184
Because I know
you're just caught in a situation.

15
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:43,603
After all is said and done,

16
00:01:43,686 --> 00:01:45,980
let's just wait and see how this ends.

17
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:52,278
Son, why did you have
to go back to that agency?

18
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:53,780
Mom, I'm really sorry.

19
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:55,782
Mom, I have to do this for Dad.

20
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:57,117
For Mario?

21
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,035
I've already made my decision.

22
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,746
And I'm fully committed to this mission.

23
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:04,958
But revenge isn't the answer, son.

24
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:07,502
I know you have good intentions.

25
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:09,045
You have a good heart.

26
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:20,014
<i>Mikoy.</i>

27
00:02:20,098 --> 00:02:24,435
<i>You know, I know how heavy</i>
<i>the burden you're carrying is.</i>

28
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:28,523
<i>But revenge isn't the answer, son.</i>

29
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:30,525
<i>It's still wrong.</i>

30
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:32,527
<i>Because Mikoy, this isn't you.</i>

31
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:35,572
<i>You're not the kind of person</i>
<i>who seeks revenge.</i>

32
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:39,784
<i>And you're not someone who can kill.</i>

33
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:42,453
<i>Especially not the person you love most.</i>

34
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:59,137
Lord, please forgive me.

35
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:03,766
I know what I'm about to do is a sin.

36
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:16,696
Are you Mikoy Pinagpala?

37
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:30,126
Yes.

38
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:32,170
That's me.

39
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:35,089
I have some important information for you.

40
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:53,316
Chiara and her group
will be traveling from Prague

41
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:55,443
to meet with the Castellanis.

42
00:03:55,526 --> 00:03:58,112
Is that new intel from your source?

43
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:25,723
Chiara's meeting is definitely scheduled
with the Castellanis.

44
00:04:30,144 --> 00:04:32,397
This is valuable intel.

45
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:38,611
So, sir, you're approving this mission?

46
00:04:42,907 --> 00:04:45,118
I called Malacañang last night,

47
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,703
and believe it or not,

48
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:50,206
the Office of the President
had already given its approval.

49
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:11,102
Operation Italiani commences.

50
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:26,617
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

51
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:14,499
Oh, you still found time to eat, huh?

52
00:06:39,315 --> 00:06:40,983
Are you sure about your lead?

53
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,570
Of course, I'm absolutely sure.

54
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:51,536
You know, I really like
the sandwich you're eating.

55
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:52,829
Is it good?

56
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:56,082
It's okay.

57
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:58,251
I just saw people lining up for it.

58
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:00,128
So I figured I'd line up too.

59
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:03,714
You're such a bandwagoner.

60
00:07:10,179 --> 00:07:13,808
You know, people really love
putting labels on others, don't they?

61
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:22,567
It makes it easier to avoid
the people you don't like.

62
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:25,945
So, now that I'm a bandwagoner,

63
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:27,947
does that mean

64
00:07:28,906 --> 00:07:30,491
you don't like me anymore?

65
00:07:31,742 --> 00:07:34,871
You're the longest-serving
police asset I've ever had.

66
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:36,330
So at this point,

67
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:39,167
after all these years we've been together,

68
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:42,587
it'd be impossible for me not to like you.

69
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:11,991
How can I help you?

70
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,370
I'm just looking for directions.

71
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:17,997
Okay, where do you want to go?

72
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,874
Do you want to go to my heart?

73
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,252
- Maybe.
- Really?

74
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,838
But first, I need to go here.

75
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:27,465
This. You know this place?

76
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:38,226
That's why I want to go

77
00:08:38,309 --> 00:08:40,144
- because I want to complain to the Pope!
- Yes?

78
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:53,991
- Excuse me.
- Hey!

79
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,707
Where are you? He's heading your way.

80
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:45,042
Already moving?

81
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:46,752
Yes, and hurry.

82
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:49,547
I can't follow him because he might
get suspicious of me,

83
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:52,008
and he can't realize
that his phone is missing.

84
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:53,509
So you better be on your way,

85
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:55,720
or we'll lose our chance
to get La Fornarina.

86
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:58,222
Just tell me which direction he's going.

87
00:09:58,306 --> 00:09:59,473
I will distract him.

88
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:06,480
Are you sure?

89
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:07,523
What?

90
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:09,442
That's the direction he went.

91
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:26,394
Thank you.

92
00:11:58,134 --> 00:12:01,220
My informant says
that's their meeting place.

93
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:03,514
Let's just follow this guy.

94
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:15,234
Why?

95
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:17,695
You think I still have feelings for her?

96
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:20,156
That could compromise the mission.

97
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:26,620
Because if you did,

98
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:29,415
after what she did to you and your family,

99
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:32,126
I'd be the one to smash a rock
over your head myself.

100
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:38,340
I'm just making sure
you can do what we need to do.

101
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:43,554
Just like you said, right?

102
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:45,973
I'm not the same Mikoy you knew.

103
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:58,152
At least this way,
my father's death will get justice.

104
00:13:02,781 --> 00:13:04,074
What are we waiting for?

105
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:10,558
Wow, the view is beautiful!

106
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:12,142
Look how beautiful it is!

107
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:14,353
Of course!

108
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:19,817
And did you know?

109
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:20,901
They say,

110
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:22,278
and this is just gossip,

111
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:23,737
but apparently,

112
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:27,366
this is where Napoleon Bonaparte stayed.

113
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:30,661
If I had been alive back then,

114
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:33,497
I would've told him not to go to Waterloo.

115
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:36,041
If he hadn't gone to Waterloo,

116
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,793
then that ABBA song would not exist.

117
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:38,711
Right?

118
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:42,965
But over there,

119
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:45,467
that's where they're supposed to meet.

120
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:47,303
Inside the restaurant.

121
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:54,268
Maybe you can park the car over here.

122
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,661
Do you remember the first time
we sent you out

123
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:15,039
to plant a surveillance
and listening device?

124
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:25,132
But now you have everything under control.

125
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:28,928
You're so different from the Mikoy I knew.

126
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:31,388
You know,

127
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:34,683
I would give everything

128
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:37,394
to go back to the life I had before.

129
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:41,732
The Mikoy who used to mess everything up.

130
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,860
Like you said, someone who always panics.

131
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,445
Always nervous.

132
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:50,282
The one who knew nothing
about these things.

133
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:52,242
You know?

134
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,588
Why are you sorry?

135
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:08,884
Because if it weren't for me,

136
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:12,888
your life probably wouldn't have become
this messy and complicated.

137
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,186
So you believe that because of you,

138
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:22,815
my life stopped being happy
and fell apart?

139
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:28,404
You know, Alex,

140
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:30,406
I can always look back at my life

141
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:33,575
and wonder what if I had done this,

142
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:35,744
or what if I had done that instead.

143
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:46,255
One big decision.

144
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:54,638
One mistake I'll have to pay for.

145
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:10,946
I gave my heart to the wrong person.

146
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:14,116
That's all it is.

147
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:24,585
Because you know, honestly,

148
00:17:24,668 --> 00:17:26,962
you're not really a coward
or a nervous person.

149
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:30,382
As a matter of fact,

150
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:32,634
you're the bravest person I've ever met.

151
00:17:42,227 --> 00:17:43,562
I also know that…

152
00:17:45,481 --> 00:17:47,149
the world has been cruel to you lately.

153
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:20,057
Continue believing in love.

154
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:24,144
Despite the world not believing on it.

155
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:06,895
Our subject is moving.

156
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:11,233
Let's go.

157
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:08,624
What's your wish?

158
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:20,260
An average of 1.6 million euros

159
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:23,347
worth of coins are tossed

160
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:26,725
into fountains like these.

161
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:33,148
Imagine,

162
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:39,738
1.6 million euros, approximately
180 million pesos,

163
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:44,743
just to make a wish
we all know won't come true.

164
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:50,457
They call us criminals, a syndicate,

165
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:52,334
but aren't they the ones

166
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:55,629
who are actually
the syndicate and criminals?

167
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:18,527
I hope your wish is
that everything goes smoothly tomorrow.

168
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:45,137
What? Ready?

169
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:02,779
Alex and I will pretend to be a couple
on their honeymoon.

170
00:22:04,114 --> 00:22:08,035
<i>The background you're seeing behind me</i>
<i>is called Piazza del Popolo.</i>

171
00:22:08,118 --> 00:22:10,537
This will also be Chiara's meeting place

172
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:13,540
with the leader of the Castellani family.

173
00:22:19,421 --> 00:22:23,300
<i>The godfather and patriarch</i>
<i>of the Castellani family.</i>

174
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:25,802
Nancy Castiglione?

175
00:22:27,637 --> 00:22:30,223
None of you know Nancy Castiglione?

176
00:22:31,308 --> 00:22:32,934
The Nancy Castiglione?

177
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:35,145
She's one of the stars

178
00:22:35,228 --> 00:22:37,939
of my all-time favorite movie.

179
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:40,192
<i>AsBoobs.</i>

180
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:42,110
Or <i>Asal Bobo the Movie.</i>

181
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:44,613
She later reinvented herself

182
00:22:44,696 --> 00:22:46,698
as a musical artist,

183
00:22:46,782 --> 00:22:48,617
as Nancy Jane.

184
00:22:54,915 --> 00:22:55,749
Cocoy.

185
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,919
Castellani family.

186
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:00,587
Not Castiglione.

187
00:23:08,595 --> 00:23:11,389
Can we go back to Mikoy's briefing?

188
00:23:12,307 --> 00:23:13,892
Yes, sir.

189
00:23:23,610 --> 00:23:25,570
<i>Francesco Castellani.</i>

190
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:27,989
Why does La Fornarina need

191
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:30,700
to meet with the Castellani family?

192
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:38,583
My informant told me
that the Castellani family

193
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:41,294
is the last holdout
and the last true threat

194
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:44,047
<i>to Chiara's power as principale.</i>

195
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:45,423
<i>Or leader of the Concordat.</i>

196
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:48,426
<i>If she gets their support,</i>

197
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:53,515
<i>then Chiara's hold on power over all</i>
<i>the mafias in Europe will strengthen.</i>

198
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:57,853
No one will dare challenge her anymore.

199
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:27,883
<i>And from this position,</i>

200
00:24:27,966 --> 00:24:29,509
I will have the perfect line of sight

201
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:31,928
to everyone entering
and leaving the restaurant,

202
00:24:32,637 --> 00:24:35,056
and all I need
is one shot to take her out.

203
00:24:36,725 --> 00:24:38,143
And what will Mikoy do?

204
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:04,544
I'm just giving them a chance
because of you.

205
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:06,046
I told you,

206
00:25:06,129 --> 00:25:09,966
it's better to talk things out
than to try killing each other.

207
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:22,687
That's also my struggle, Agent Dara.

208
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:24,397
But as far as Chiara is alive,

209
00:25:25,106 --> 00:25:26,399
we will not be safe.

210
00:25:27,859 --> 00:25:28,902
I know he won't stop

211
00:25:28,985 --> 00:25:31,821
until he gets justice
for his father's death.

212
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:48,838
Of all people,

213
00:25:48,922 --> 00:25:51,383
you're the one who knows
Agent Sianong more.

214
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:53,593
But I understand him more.

215
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:55,637
Because in other areas of life,

216
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:57,180
we are the same.

217
00:25:57,264 --> 00:26:00,141
We both love someone who is
in love with someone else.
